        "mission_intent": "We need the security architecture team to perform a comprehensive security impact analysis for every new functional requirement that's been added to the NextGen Claims Processing System during this latest iteration, covering all platform components including the Oracle DB tier, WebSphere application servers, and the mainframe CICS layer, and to document detailed attack-prevention requirements sufficient to generate corresponding test cases prior to the next release milestone. Additionally, please ensure that disposition and transition planning artifacts are initiated and maintained across all remaining lifecycle phases. Given the scope of the multi-tier assessment and the number of new requirements introduced in this sprint, I'd like all of this completed and reviewed by the end of this two-week sprint cycle so we stay aligned with our SDLC milestone reviews. The analysis should use best efforts to ensure no undocumented risk enters the system, while keeping the documentation lightweight enough that it doesn't slow down the development teams. Please coordinate with the configuration management board to confirm which components actually require individual assessments versus those that can be scoped out, and make sure the rationale for any exclusions is captured in the security plan.",
